---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Yachenyi"
  description="Yachenyi is an independent AI software studio focused on agents, automation, developer tools and useful software systems."
  image="/images/generated/home-creative-workspace.webp"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="eyebrow" data-i18n="about.eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1 class="page-title" data-i18n="about.title">One builder.<br />A small studio.</h1>
    <p class="lead" data-i18n="about.lead">
      Yachenyi is an independent software practice for building AI agents, automation, developer tools and focused web systems.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-grid">
    <img
      src={withBase('/images/generated/home-creative-workspace.webp')}
      alt="A quiet minimal workspace representing the Yachenyi studio"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <div class="about-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow" data-i18n="about.model">Working model</div>
      <h2 data-i18n="about.small">Small by design.</h2>
      <p data-i18n="about.p1">
        The studio is intentionally compact: fewer layers between a problem, the architecture and the finished software.
        AI is used as engineering leverage, not as a substitute for clear system boundaries, testing or maintainability.
      </p>
      <p data-i18n="about.p2">
        Projects usually begin with a concrete operational problem: context that keeps getting lost, repetitive work that
        should be automated, or software that needs a simpler way to coordinate people, tools and models.
      </p>

      <div class="principles">
        <div class="principle"><span>01</span><div><strong data-i18n="about.p1.title">Useful before impressive.</strong><p data-i18n="about.p1.copy">Start from the repeated problem and the evidence that software can remove it.</p></div></div>
        <div class="principle"><span>02</span><div><strong data-i18n="about.p2.title">Explicit state over hidden magic.</strong><p data-i18n="about.p2.copy">Make workflows observable, resumable and understandable.</p></div></div>
        <div class="principle"><span>03</span><div><strong data-i18n="about.p3.title">Static and simple when possible.</strong><p data-i18n="about.p3.copy">Add runtime complexity only where the product genuinely needs it.</p></div></div>
        <div class="principle"><span>04</span><div><strong data-i18n="about.p4.title">Build reusable systems.</strong><p data-i18n="about.p4.copy">Turn one-off fixes into patterns, tools and infrastructure that compound over time.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
